			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4851595">
									

<p>I have been told that necroposting is fine if you are adding onto the existing conversation which is at hand in a non-spammy matter, so I will be adding onto what <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/wizzblizz" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6760712); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6760712&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608706166" alt="WizzBlizz" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6760712)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/wizzblizz" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6760712); return false;">WizzBlizz</a></span> has previously stated.</p>
<p>This feels like there is simply to much lore here for me to completely care. When I first found the canon &quot;In Memoria, Adytum&quot;, I was curious on how Sarkicism works in lore. I went to this hub and immediately became overwhelmed with how much information was here, leading me to assume that I should wait on reading. When I came back, I began reading and merely felt <em>bored.</em> All this lore within this GOI page really wants me looking towards the other works because any intrigue is answered in the same GOI. I feel no reason to learn more after reading through this initially. When I look towards a GOI hub, I expect to see enough information for me to get a grasp on the GOI itself, yet want to look to learn more towards the GOI (alongside contribution information). To put it simply, I feel like this hub should be having me want to read more of the works. I still do plan on reading more under In Memoria, Adytum, but as a whole, this lowers my opinion on sarkicism articles. Simply to much here.</p>
<p>My biggest advice for improvement on this hub page is to cut down on what is already there. The amount of works under this GOI alone makes me feel afraid to start because I am unsure where to begin.</p>
<p>However, as it stands, this hub earns my -1.</p>

