				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/deltathree" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6974566); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6974566&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608709644" alt="DeltaThree" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6974566)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/deltathree" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6974566); return false;" >DeltaThree</a></span> <span class="odate time_1608701542 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">23 Dec 2020 05:32</span>
																	<br/>
						in discussion <a href="/forum/c-891087/help:questions-desk">Writing Help / Help: Questions Desk</a> &raquo;
						<a href="/forum/t-13952385/my-first-scp-article">My first SCP article</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4851557">
									

<p>I am new and I have been thinking of a few ideas for SCP articles, but now that I have my big shot I don't which one you guys want to see first, so before I head in for the greenlight, does anyone wanna weigh in on which one you want to read that I should pitch first?</p>
<p>Playing with Fire - silly putty like substance that is plasma at room temperature, from Dr. Wondertainment.<br />
Vampire Bodega - mini-mart where everything seems to be free, but actually draws blood from customers, not noticeable unless the customer comes more than twice a week. May be part of Marshall, Carter and Dark.<br />
Cryovampire - cryogenically preserved person who was successfully revived, but now absorbs heat energy. Must be kept in a room heated to 98.6 degrees Farenheit at which point the ambient temperature neutralizes the anomaly, but as soon as it is exposed to lower temperatures it reverts to a savage that freezes anything it touches.<br />
Alzoidian - a cephalopod like alien life form native to the red spot of Jupiter. Exists in symbiosis with a fungus and another species that resembles a manta ray. Still not quite sure how to explain how the foundation even acquired it…<br />
Scapegoats - the cursed goats that carry the sins of the nation of Israel according to an ancient ritual.<br />
Swine Legion - the cursed swine possessed by demons exorcised by Jesus.</p>
<p>SPC-2806: cybernetics for pugilists who lost limbs in shark attacks so that they may once again punch sharks.</p>

