<p>Thank you for your feedback! This is a completely fair criticism, and something I actually thought of after posting.</p>
<p>A few details were left out due to the word count limit—the singularity does not affect gravity planetside due to its anomalous properties. There is no scientific explanation. I definitely need to fix the stone tablet concept though.</p>
<p>Secondly, displacing the singularity to another universe was considered and is ultimately what they may end up doing (it's left ambiguous at the end of the file, stated that disposal through use of SCP-1437 was requested, but not if it was approved).</p>
<p>I'm not quite sure what you're saying in #1. Could you clarify?</p>
<p>If these issues in the article are resolved (and/or I cover how the SCP is disposed of and label it as &quot;neutralized&quot;, does this change your opinion on the concept?</p>

